<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Burebista</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/44-bce">44 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Burebista was a king of the Getae and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dacians">Dacians</a> who, from about 82 BCE, united their tribes into a powerful kingdom, aided by the high priest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deceneus">Deceneus</a>. He extended his realm from the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>, defeating the Boii and Scordisci and sacking Greek cities such as Olbia and Histria. He was murdered in 44 BCE, and his kingdom split apart.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/burebista.jpg" alt="Burebista" width="212" height="336" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Jokes_Free4Me · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Burebista_cropped.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
